        <mxCell id="NKc8lnMmxln-4O3GPi_p-18" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;autosize=1;resizable=0;" value="Partitioned by PageID" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="140" x="30" y="690" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NKc8lnMmxln-4O3GPi_p-19" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;autosize=1;resizable=0;" value="Partitioned by PageID" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="140" x="280" y="690" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NKc8lnMmxln-4O3GPi_p-20" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=#82b366;fillColor=#d5e8d4;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;autosize=1;resizable=0;" value="Top K Aggregation is to be precomputed and cached to Redis for Fast Read&lt;div&gt;Flink consumer will&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;do Windows Aggregation via batching. Flink can wait till time T for events to arrive and batch. (Tumbling Window). Also it make sense to aggrgate at window level if we want to do Sliding Window.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Option1 : Flink to update Event DB and a cron job can run periodically to precompute and store in Redis.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Reads to EventDB can be optimised by having individual views say perHour, per Minute, perDay to read from till Redis doesn&#39;t have precomputed entry.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Option2 : Compute top K (last hour, day, month) Natively in Flink and store to Redis Directly. We don&#39;t need DB altogether.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;SLIDING WINDOW:&lt;br&gt;Option 1 only does Tumbling Windows. For SW, we will have to derive it by using Tumble View Tables.&lt;br&gt;Also it makes practical sense to keep just Last Hour as SW and rest as TB.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="1160" x="50" y="370" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
